# comms-bridge logs: the two-log coordination channel between the legacy
# system's agent and this fleet (docs/cross-project/comms-bridge-spec.md).
# Coordination traffic is working material — anything durable in a log is
# promoted to a committed file, and the spec rules the active logs stay out
# of git regardless.
bridge/*.log.md

# macOS Finder directory metadata: created by the operating system in any
# directory a user browses, belongs to nobody's work
.DS_Store

# Obsidian per-vault state (UI panes, workspace, plugin caches) — quarry-proven pattern
.obsidian/

# walk-me-through tier-3 anchors: machine-local tmp ledgers, deleted at walk close (skill: .claude/skills/walk-me-through)
walk-ledgers/

# per-agent identity files: one agent, one worktree, never committed (ruled on nedschorus#45)
CLAUDE.local.md

# instruction-file-guard override marker: consumed per approved change (.claude/hooks/instruction-file-guard.py)
.walk-approved

# session-location-write-guard override marker: same consumed-per-write contract
# (.claude/hooks/session-location-write-guard.py)
.location-write-approved

# backup-write-guard override marker, LEGACY: the lane was removed 2026-08-17 —
# backups are never agent-writable — but a stale marker from before the removal
# must still never be committed (.claude/hooks/backup-and-snapshot-write-guard.py)
.backup-write-approved

# Python bytecode caches: the test scripts import modules by path, which
# writes these beside the sources
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# md-review grid output: machine-local review evidence, never committed
# (user-ruled 2026-08-14). The founding plan's disposal rule already covers
# this class — "an evidence archive or reference file DELETES, with the
# extracted decisions memorialized in their governing documents and a
# `git show <sha>:<path>` recovery pointer" — and it had never been applied
# here, so the directory grew to 69% of everything the repository tracked.
# A review's findings belong in the document it reviewed; the transcripts
# that produced them are working material, deleted when the work they served
# lands. Everything deleted stays retrievable: git show db917b5:<path>
md-review-records/

# sanity-check records: the second review instrument's output
# (scripts/sanity-check-attacks.py) — same class and disposal as
# md-review-records: machine-local working material, deleted when the work it
# served lands; git history is the archive
sanity-check-records/

# ghi-info's local GHI mirror (nedschorus#46, docs/issues/46-ghi-info-agent-design.md
# § The GHI mirror): derived from GitHub by scripts/ghi-mirror-refresh.py,
# regenerable on any machine — a committed mirror would pollute the history the
# user reads with pure derived churn (the design's own "Deliberately not in
# version 1" table). Includes the ask wrapper's session state
# (.ghi-info-state.json) alongside it.
ghi-mirror/
.ghi-info-state.json
.ghi-info-state.lock
# A contended ask publishes into a private mirror it removes in a `finally`,
# which a SIGHUP skips — reachable when the Mac side's ssh timeout kills a
# box-side ask mid-run. Each leftover is a corpus-sized copy, which is the
# class nedschorus#50 (worktree file hygiene) closed a ruling on.
.ghi-mirror-throwaway-*/
.ghi-info-state.json.tmp
